Cuboidz <Dieter.Be...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> 1) How thoroughly do you search each dungeon level before continuing
> to the next?

As long as I have found the up and down stairs, maybe thorough
maybe not.  If there are no messages telling me about features
I have not yet seen I don't spend extra time searching.

> Do you try to discover all secret rooms (including shops
> and vaults)?

If there's a vault I mark it as such.  Maybe writing in the dust,
maybe a #named rock dropped near the down stairs.  Other
special rooms I do make a point of searching for them.

> Also, how many times do you search one spot before
> deciding nothing's there (using "n[number]s")?

First pass I do 1 s per move and that ends up being 3 per
square.  Second pass I'll do 2 s per move and at places I
think should have a hidden door 5s.  Not lacking a shop
I don't put all that much effort into finding a vault unless I
have some reason for the money or I think I might be in
Ludios territory.

> 2) Is "leveling" a good idea in nethack, e.g. running around until you
> see a monster to kill (to gain experience)?

Levels 1-4 yes.  The deeper you go the less true that becomes.
Since I am often XP=9+ by the time I exit the mines and each
new level takes exponential points I completely give up on it
after the mines.

But notice - Levels are better for some classes worse for other
classes, and entirely a matter of tastes.  Because each level
opens up another skill slot there is some incentive to level up;
because each level means facing stronger monsters there is
some incentive to not level up.  But somewhere after XP=12 or
so the number of points needed gets so high killing monsters
is no longer the way to advance.

> 3) Do you make the effort of picking up every single item, even if you
> don't need it, in order to sell it in a shop - unless the load would
> burden you, or course? Even more, do you run back for items you left
> because you couldn't carry any more items (for the same purpose of
> selling them)?

Once I find the down stairs I do shuttle items to a stash there.
Before entering the mines I do shuttle everything down to mine
town for BUC ID to make sure I have the best randomly found
armor I could get.  Often below mine town I shuttle items up to
mine town.

But once I exit the mines deciding to shuttle items deeper and
deeper depends on where I want my final stash and how many
stashes I want.  Does my character have easy level teleport to
several stashes, that effects my stash strategy.



